<title>ITALY: Italy restores Treasury five pct INA voting limit.</title>
<headline>Italy restores Treasury five pct INA voting limit.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian government has restored the five percent voting ceiling limit that the Treasury has in partly-privatisated insurance group Istituto Nazionale Assicurazioni (INA).</p>
<p>An amendment to the 1997 budget package was approved late on Wednesday by the Senate finance and budget commission to limit the Treasury's voting rights in INA to five percent, although the Treasury currently holds 34 percent of the insurer's stock.</p>
<p>The Treasury's stake is set to fall as INA bonds become convertible into the group's shares.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
